dentifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/values(of:)-8gzq9"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix\/values(of:)-8gzq9"]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"externalID":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule08OrientedaB0V6values2of14GraphProtocols10EdgeValuesVyACxGAF0I3MapVyxG_tlF","extendedModule":"IncidenceMatrixModule","roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","remoteSource":{"fileName":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix+PropertyGraph.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix+PropertyGraph.swift#L139"},"modules":[{"name":"IncidenceMatrixModule"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"values"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"of"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"EdgeMap","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols7EdgeMapV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":">) -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"EdgeValues","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols10EdgeValuesV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","preciseIdentifier":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule08OrientedaB0V"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"title":"values(of:)","role":"symbol"},"references":{"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/OrientedIncidenceMatrix":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The oriented incidence matrix of a directed hypergraph: entry (v, p) is −1 when ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a source","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of column ","type":"text"},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", +1 when it is a target, and 0 otherwise. Gallo, Longo, Pallottino and Nguyen","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(1993) define a directed hypergraph’s matrix this way (aᵢⱼ = −1 for a tail node, 1 for a head","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"node); a directed graph’s edge is the column with one source and one target, the matrix of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"spectral graph theory (B·Bᵀ = L, Godsil–Royle §8.3) and NetworkX’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidence_matrix(oriented=True)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". It conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedHypergraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hypergraphs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"algorithms (B- and F-connection, components, the clique expansion) run on it unchanged; it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not a ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/EdgeMap":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A handle to a map from edge positions to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Value","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" attached to a graph (LEMON’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"ArcMap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"returned by ","type":"text"},{"code":"PropertyGraph.addEdgeMap(default:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". It holds no values: read and write them","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through the graph, ","type":"text"},{"code":"graph[handle, ofEdgeAt: position]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". It is valid on the graph that added it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and on every copy of that graph, until ","type":"text"},{"code":"removeEdgeMap(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; on another graph it traps.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"EdgeMap","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/EdgeMap","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EdgeMap","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EdgeMap","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/edgemap"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/EdgeValues":{"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/edgevalues","title":"EdgeValues","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A snapshot of an edge map’s values, read by edge position like an array: what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PropertyGraph.values(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns, after "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Dictionary.Values"},{"type":"text","text":". It holds the map’s storage, not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the graph, so later mutations of the graph or the map do not show through."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EdgeValues"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EdgeValues"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/EdgeValues"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/OrientedIncidenceMatrix/values(of:)-8gzq9":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/values(of:)-8gzq9","kind":"s